# A fighter whose wake-up ends turns to face its opponent before it reads a buffered reversal. p1 sweeps p2 (2c,
# knockdown) and air-dashes over it while it gets up (wake-up on frames 61-72): p1 is still in front when the wake-up
# starts and passes p2 on frame 64, above its pushbox. p2 can't turn during the wake-up and inputs a 623c toward p1,
# to its right: 4, 2, 1 relative to its old facing. On its first free frame (73) it turns right first, and the 623c
# comes out toward p1.
setup: p1 character testman
setup: p2 character testman
# The geometry below is Testman's long jump (jump velocity 20000); pinned so jump tuning in data/ can't move it.
setup: p1 stat jump_velocity 20000
setup: p1 x = -20000
setup: p2 x = 20000

frame 1: p1 2c
frame 49: p1 9
frame 58: p1 dash                        # air dash, at 90000 up
frame 70: p2 4, 2, 1c                    # right, down, down-right + c: a 623c toward p1

frame 9: expect p2 state = knockdown
frame 61: expect p2 state = wake_up
frame 61: expect p1 x = 19000            # in front of p2 (43000)
frame 64: expect p1 x = 52000            # past p2
frames 61-72: expect p2 state = wake_up
frames 61-72: expect p2 facing = left
frame 73: expect p2 move = 623c
frame 73: expect p2 facing = right
frame 74: expect p2 x = 48000            # 623c moves forward 2500 per frame: right, toward p1
